{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:46e91159ca0483c5","name":"Trandoshan Mercenary","source":{"id":"source:reference-46e91159ca0483c5","title":"Trandoshan Mercenary","revision":25530,"timestamp":"2024-11-27T01:11:25Z","sha256":"60c7446d1bda3b1e6479bb356de73d0a9a819e7d8f4712a73b3c4c5963b328f9","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=25530","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Trandoshan%20Mercenary&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-46e91159ca0483c5","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Web Enhancements"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Web_Enhancements"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Star Wars Miniatures Previews"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Star_Wars_Miniatures_Previews"},")"]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The reptilian ",{"tag":"a","children":["Trandoshans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Trandoshans"}," are known for their great strength and warlike natures, so it's no surprise that many of them take up careers as bounty hunters or mercenaries. The physical traits of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Trandoshans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Trandoshans"}," make them natural warriors. Their supersensitive eyes can see into the infrared spectrum, allowing nighttime operations without relying on equipment whose energy signature might be detected by enemy sensors. Their tough scales make them particularly resistant to attacks, and their natural ability to regenerate lost limbs ensures that they can avoid early retirement if a mission goes bad. Finally, their great strength makes them brutal in close quarters.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Trandoshan Mercenaries are very common in almost any era, and they are particularly active during ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"},". For example, Delta Squad (Republic Commandos Boss, Fixer, Scorch, and Sev) ran afoul of Trandoshan Mercenaries that had captured The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Prosecutor"]},", an ",{"tag":"a","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Acclamator"]},"-Class Assault Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Acclamator-Class_Assault_Ship"},", and later found them supporting Separatist operations on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Kashyyyk"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Kashyyyk","referenceId":"reference:0886d73261c13472"},". While most Trandoshan Mercenaries have no trouble finding work, it's not uncommon to find some who turn to slaving as a means of supplementing their income.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Trandoshan Mercenary Statistics (CL 2)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Trandoshan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Trandoshan","referenceId":"reference:7462eb9a66c70e5d"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 6\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +7; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darkvision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darkvision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +2\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic, Dosh\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 15 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 13), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 10, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"h